of fixed volume. The animals were female only of the same genetics and about
the same size and development stage. Instead of obtaining increasing bio-pho-
ton emission with increasing number of animals, Galle observed in several ex-
periments maxima and minima of photon emission. One of the minima corre-
sponds  to  a  ‘natural’  distance which  is  preferred  by  the  animals if  they  are
living in freedom. It has been argued that an interpretation of the results by a

